                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I haven't played this game in over two years because i was so frustrated that after an update, my save data was deleted, and i lost my patience, since i made a lot of progress, and there was no recovery method. and it looked like the game had a history of doing this. Fast Forward to 2026, supposedly the game is going 1.0, and some other junk, so i just decided to give it a try again. It felt like i was hit with a freight train of just... a completely different game wearing the original game's skin. I really don't like it.\n\nThe game starts out with a new lengthy opening cutscene with some romantic interest or someone begging you to not do a job. And then there's an AI voice just yapping at you constantly. This is overly talkative already for a game that used to just be about Getting To The Orange Door, and that was it. get gear, get out, whatever challenges in-between. And now there's inventory management. What????? Why????? why does this game thats supposed to be fast-paced and about just upgrading your gear as you go need this??? This just doesn't feel like the same game that I played and enjoyed two years ago. i also don't recall the card-based skill system or whatever that makes you need to open R6 Siege-style packs, but that just also feels excessive. I just want to go fast and open doors and shoot things, I never came to this game to look for a ton of dialog or \"more\" from how i collect things.",
